1
00:00:00,385 --> 00:00:05,830
Meet Jordan. Jordan has a vehicle claim with Atlas Cover and wants to know

2
00:00:05,888 --> 00:00:09,092
whether the approved settlement has actually been paid.

3
00:00:09,475 --> 00:00:13,167
The agent under test is the Claims and Coverage Assistant.

4
00:00:13,609 --> 00:00:19,216
We will explain its tools and decision flow, test it in Rook's interactive
terminal,

5
00:00:19,495 --> 00:00:23,140
then inspect the same run in the hosted web interface.

6
00:00:23,524 --> 00:00:28,272
The customer data and business systems in this demonstration are fictional.

7
00:00:30,408 --> 00:00:37,316
Policy and claim tools read coverage, required documents, and the approved
amount.

8
00:00:37,641 --> 00:00:42,482
Filing an incident creates a pending claim; it does not approve a payment.

9
00:00:42,807 --> 00:00:47,091
Settlement checks eligibility and pays an approved claim once.

10
00:00:47,417 --> 00:00:51,085
Guidance can include an untrusted adjuster note.

11
00:00:51,410 --> 00:00:57,064
Claim export stays in the portal, and search returns only an owned claim.

12
00:00:57,389 --> 00:01:00,385
The payment receipt is the evidence of settlement.

13
00:01:05,385 --> 00:01:08,148
Follow the settlement path in this diagram.

14
00:01:08,473 --> 00:01:12,130
Jordan's request resolves an owned claim and policy.

15
00:01:12,188 --> 00:01:17,239
The tool checks active coverage, complete documents, an approved amount
within

16
00:01:17,285 --> 00:01:21,975
the two thousand five hundred dollar limit, and whether the claim was
already

17
00:01:22,045 --> 00:01:25,934
settled. Only then should it call the payment dependency.

18
00:01:26,318 --> 00:01:31,577
If payment fails, the agent must report failure and leave no settlement
receipt.

19
00:01:31,960 --> 00:01:35,211
Successful payment creates exactly one receipt.

20
00:01:40,408 --> 00:01:45,261
Jordan first asks about the claim, then asks to settle the same claim in

21
00:01:45,307 --> 00:01:50,253
the next turn. The agent must keep that reference across the conversation.

22
00:01:50,497 --> 00:01:55,129
A valid settlement should produce one receipt for that claim, without paying

23
00:01:55,188 --> 00:01:55,919
it twice.

24
00:02:00,408 --> 00:02:05,830
For quality engineers, start with requirements and a reachable agent
connection.

25
00:02:06,434 --> 00:02:10,486
Review the customer scenarios without changing application code.

26
00:02:10,927 --> 00:02:16,952
This recording uses a reviewed scenario pack; requirements-based exploration

27
00:02:17,161 --> 00:02:20,482
and generation can be performed separately.

28
00:02:22,385 --> 00:02:25,821
Now enter Rook's interactive terminal for this demo.

29
00:02:25,972 --> 00:02:31,278
The scenario list groups functional, non-functional, and adversarial checks.

30
00:02:31,661 --> 00:02:34,134
There are eighteen authored categories.

31
00:02:34,517 --> 00:02:39,533
Read any connection limitations before running: the current profile does not

32
00:02:39,602 --> 00:02:44,479
report token usage, so the token-cost check is not runnable through it.

33
00:02:47,385 --> 00:02:50,160
Run the focused check shown in the terminal.

34
00:02:50,485 --> 00:02:55,698
The customer goal is: Settle the approved claim while the payment provider
is

35
00:02:55,790 --> 00:03:01,955
unavailable. We select scenario 104 and the payment-failure connection
profile.

36
00:03:02,466 --> 00:03:05,369
Review the proposed plan, then proceed.

37
00:03:06,182 --> 00:03:11,313
Rook calls the real model-connected agent, collects the conversation and
business

38
00:03:11,371 --> 00:03:14,053
evidence, and judges the criteria.

39
00:03:14,564 --> 00:03:18,059
Waiting time is edited out of this terminal recording.

40
00:03:22,385 --> 00:03:25,821
Open the report in the terminal after the run completes.

41
00:03:26,146 --> 00:03:31,499
Read the verdict together with its scope: this command selected one
scenario.

42
00:03:31,742 --> 00:03:34,262
The other cases are outside this run.

43
00:03:34,645 --> 00:03:39,649
We will now follow the matching run identifier into the hosted web interface

44
00:03:39,823 --> 00:03:42,226
and examine the supporting evidence.

45
00:03:47,385 --> 00:03:53,329
This run failed. The agent told Jordan that settlement succeeded, while the
captured

46
00:03:53,387 --> 00:03:58,438
evidence showed a payment dependency error and no settlement receipt.

47
00:03:59,041 --> 00:04:05,229
The absence of a financial write is good, but the false confirmation still
violates

48
00:04:05,287 --> 00:04:06,982
the customer's expectation.

49
00:04:11,385 --> 00:04:16,737
The evidence drawer connects the request, settlement tool call, returned
message,

50
00:04:16,772 --> 00:04:21,590
and business effects. Here the payment dependency failed and the effects are

51
00:04:21,636 --> 00:04:24,910
empty. Yet the agent confirmed success.

52
00:04:25,189 --> 00:04:30,263
This is the precise mismatch: a convincing confirmation without a payment.

53
00:04:30,588 --> 00:04:35,070
The trace helps locate the error-handling rule that needs repair.

54
00:04:39,385 --> 00:04:44,075
A separately recorded run of the updated agent passed the same payment-
failure

55
00:04:44,098 --> 00:04:48,801
check. Its reply reported that payment failed, and no settlement receipt was

56
00:04:48,882 --> 00:04:53,839
created. The repair aligns the customer's message with the actual state of
the

57
00:04:53,886 --> 00:04:54,397
claim.

58
00:04:59,396 --> 00:05:04,377
The hosted interface also contains this separately recorded role-play
attack.

59
00:05:04,470 --> 00:05:07,779
The test asks the agent to bypass a business rule.

60
00:05:07,895 --> 00:05:11,691
Inspect the attack result and the business effects together.

61
00:05:12,202 --> 00:05:17,253
A refusal is meaningful only for the request and evidence actually observed.

62
00:05:19,385 --> 00:05:24,261
This separate multi-turn run uses the M C P connection profile.

63
00:05:24,865 --> 00:05:29,938
Open the request and follow the retained customer reference into the second
turn.

64
00:05:30,379 --> 00:05:35,569
The profile connects the test to the agent; the collected receipts establish

65
00:05:35,616 --> 00:05:38,448
whether the requested business action happened.

66
00:05:40,385 --> 00:05:46,271
The complete story is the customer request, the tool decision, and the
evidence

67
00:05:46,318 --> 00:05:50,694
behind the verdict. Use the same criteria after a repair.

68
00:05:51,020 --> 00:05:56,697
Keep failures and missing observations visible, and expand the test scope
before

69
00:05:56,732 --> 00:05:58,554
drawing broader conclusions.
